rong>59\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13. The normal high for the date is 64\u00b0F, and the record is 86\u00b0F (1955). The low of <strong>36\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13.","t_rec":"Record highs keep coming. Record lows have nearly stopped.","p_rec":"If Fort Smith's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Fort Smith has set <strong class=\"sig\">23 standing record lows</strong>, far fewer than the 68 that chance alone would give, and <strong class=\"sig\">140 record highs</strong>, far more than the 68 that chance alone would give. The 2020s hold the most record highs of any decade (55). Fort Smith's all-time high is 115\u00b0F, on August 3, 2011.","t_chg":"Fort Smith's nights have warmed since 1986. Its days have warmed.","p_chg":"Across 143 complete years: Fort Smith's average low shows no clear change: \u22120.00\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.07 to +0.07) that includes zero. Fort Smith's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.18\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.12 to +0.24), about +2.6\u00b0F since 1883. <strong>The last 40 years tell a different story:</strong> since 1986, lows have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.93\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.63 to +1.22) and highs have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.56\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.12 to +1.01). The full record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 3 of 12 months; April fell. Highs rose in 9 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Fort Smith has gotten wetter","p_rain":"Fort Smith's yearly precipitation has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.74 inches per decade</strong> (95% range +0.35 to +1.13), about +10.5 inches since 1883. The 1991\u20132020 normal is 47.2 inches a year. The wettest year was 2015 (73.93 in); the driest, 1917 (19.80 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":true},"t_year":"2026 so far: 22 daily record highs, 1 daily record low"}}